        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-23T12:38:55Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(motion): merge main into 2D Adaptive Do-not-touch, keep rest precedence\n\nMerge origin/main (3fc0e017b) into the 2D Adaptive \"Do not touch\" branch\n(issue #3346). Resolve each conflict:\n\n- crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs: a shared-logic conflict. main added\n  rest-adaptive planning (#1446); the PR restructured the same closure for\n  avoid_spec (#3346). Choose option A: main's `(Some(r), _)` rest branch\n  stays first, then the PR's avoid arms under `None` rest. Rest + \"Do not\n  touch\" is planned by the rest planner and checked by `verify_avoid`,\n  which blocks the post on a `Warning::AvoidHit`. It is a feature gap, not\n  a silent gouge.\n- crates/app/src/operation/types/avoid.rs: take both operation lists.\n  `do_not_touch_applies` now accepts Adaptive2D and Finish3D. The refusal\n  names \"Trace, 2D Offset, 2D Adaptive, 3D Pocket, Face and 3D Finish\".\n- crates/app/src/mcp/tools.rs, docs/agents/mcp-tools.md: the same union in\n  the tool description.\n- crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/do_not_touch.rs: assert the union text.\n- crates/app/tests/do_not_touch_adaptive.rs: fix the Gate-map module name\n  to motion::machining2d::adaptive_avoid (drop pocket_avoid; no\n  adaptive_troch_avoid module exists).\n\nFollow-up #3702 designs a planner or a named refusal for rest + \"Do not\ntouch\".\n\nRefs #3346\nRefs #3702\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>",
